(ADR-0001) Tj
T*
(ADR-0001 HMI?PLC Interface) Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
(Parts: VC-CT-6100, VC-CT-6110, VC-CT-6120, VC-ASM-5000) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# ADR-0001 ? HMI?PLC Interface) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Context) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Vibrocore HMI runs in Node-RED on the controller \(WAGO PFC200 XTR or RevPi\).) Tj
T*
(The PLC runs in CODESYS. The two sides exchange data over Modbus TCP holding) Tj
T*
(registers \(`GVL_MODBUS`\) and publish events on MQTT \(`Mosquitto`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This ADR fixes the command semantics so that motion is hold-to-run, start and) Tj
T*
(reset are pulses, and all sides use one fault-code table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Transport) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Path | Use |) Tj
T*
(|------|-----|) Tj
T*
(| Modbus TCP port 502 on the PLC | Command and status registers \(`GVL_MODBUS`\) |) Tj
T*
(| MQTT broker service name `mosquitto` | Cycle records, alarms, HMI presence |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(MQTT topics:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Topic | Direction | Retain | Meaning |) Tj
T*
(|-------|-----------|--------|---------|) Tj
T*
(| `vibrocore/hmi/status` | HMI ? broker | yes | `online` / `offline` |) Tj
T*
(| `vibrocore/alarm` | HMI ? broker | no | Safety fault event \(JSON\) |) Tj
T*
(| `vibrocore/cycle/{id}` | logger ? broker | no | Signed cycle record \(JSON\) |) Tj
T*
(| `vibrocore/status/#` | reserved | yes | Future live status mirror |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Units in payloads use SI with a space \(example: `12 mm`, `100 Hz`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Command semantics) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Command | Register | Semantics |) Tj
T*
(|---------|----------|-----------|) Tj
T*
(| Operating mode | `%MW0` | Change accepted only while the machine is idle \(hub IDLE, no safe s) Tj
T*
(tate, no fault\). PLC writes the old mode back if the change is rejected. |) Tj
T*
(| Cycle start | `%MW1` | Edge-triggered pulse. PLC clears the register to 0 after it reads the ) Tj
T*
(rising edge. |) Tj
T*
(| Jog down / up | `%MW2` / `%MW3` | Momentary \(hold-to-run\). Do not latch to 1. |) Tj
T*
(| Jog heartbeat | `%MW33` | HMI increments this value at least every 100 ms while a jog button ) Tj
T*
(is pressed. |) Tj
T*
(| Sonic toggle | `%MW4` | Level in MANUAL mode. |) Tj
T*
(| Fault reset | `%MW5` | Edge-triggered pulse. PLC clears to 0. After E-stop: accept only a fre) Tj
T*
(sh rising edge that arrives while the E-stop circuit is healthy. Never auto-reset. |) Tj
T*
(| Lift / tilt | `%MW22`?`%MW25` | Momentary. Direction interlock and end-limit stop are in the ) Tj
T*
(actuator FBs. No motion while the hub is not IDLE. |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Jog watchdog) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. While the operator holds a jog control, the HMI writes the direction bit and) Tj
T*
(   increments `%MW33` about every 100 ms.) Tj
T*
(2. The PLC starts a 300 ms timer when the heartbeat value stops changing.) Tj
T*
(3. If the timer ends, the PLC clears jog commands and stops motion.) Tj
T*
(4. Jog must never stay at 1 without a live heartbeat.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Fault-code table \(canonical\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Used by `FB_Safety.eSafetyReason`, `GVL_MODBUS.eStatus_SafetyReason`, and the) Tj
T*
(Node-RED `SAFETY_REASON` list:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Code | Name |) Tj
T*
(|------|------|) Tj
T*
(| 0 | OK |) Tj
T*
(| 1 | ESTOP |) Tj
T*
(| 2 | LIMIT_UP |) Tj
T*
(| 3 | LIMIT_DOWN |) Tj
T*
(| 4 | HUB_ALARM |) Tj
T*
(| 5 | STONE_DETECTED |) Tj
T*
(| 6 | VFD_COMM |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Penetrometer Modbus loss uses a local FB fault flag and status force value. It) Tj
T*
(does not add a seventh safety reason to this table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Mode switch) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(`eMode` follows `%MW0` only when:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- hub state is IDLE, and) Tj
T*
(- safe state is false, and) Tj
T*
(- hub and sonic have no fault.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the HMI writes a new mode while the machine is busy, the PLC restores the) Tj
T*
(previous mode in `%MW0`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
